From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qa <qa@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: record the owner's runtime decision - a virtual
 machine, not yet written

The documents said "runtime backend: not selected". That stopped being
true on 2026-11-10: the project owner chose the class of runtime - Android
in a hardware-accelerated virtual machine, "like VirtualBox, as
BlueStacks does", not a container.

What is still open, and stated as open: which hypervisor (an existing one
- QEMU/KVM, crosvm, VirtualBox - or a monitor of our own on the KVM API).
No virtual-machine code exists in this branch; the wording keeps saying
that the engine does not start Android.

Documentation and one header comment only. No code path changes:
make verify - 386 tests, 0 failures, verify: OK.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
