 # LynxDroid: standalone Android gaming engine architecture
 
-**Status:** architecture draft for a Linux-hosted Android gaming runtime. **No runtime backend is selected.** Waydroid was a prototype candidate and has been removed by the project owner's decision of 2026-11-10: LynxDroid must not depend on Waydroid. Do not reintroduce it without a new explicit decision. This document does not declare compatibility with every game or with BlueStacks. It also does not authorize or implement a connection to the legacy Android agent.
+**Status:** architecture draft for a Linux-hosted Android gaming runtime. **No runtime backend is implemented.** Two decisions of the project owner, both of 2026-11-10: Waydroid, a prototype candidate, has been removed — LynxDroid must not depend on it, and it must not be reintroduced without a new explicit decision; and the Android runtime is to be a **hardware-accelerated virtual machine** ("like VirtualBox, as BlueStacks does"), not a container. No virtual-machine code exists in this branch, and which hypervisor to build on (an existing one — QEMU/KVM, crosvm, VirtualBox — or a monitor of our own on the KVM API) is still the owner's open question. This document does not declare compatibility with every game or with BlueStacks. It also does not authorize or implement a connection to the legacy Android agent.
 
